    "body": "doc: describe dropping unused tables from static builds\n\nAdds a short README section: compile with `-ffunction-sections -fdata-sections` and link with `-Wl,--gc-sections`, so a static build drops the precomputed tables and code a program never calls. A verification-only program should use `secp256k1_context_static`, because a context from `secp256k1_context_create` keeps the signing table linked in.\n\nAddresses the last open item of #1065 (the other items are checked). real-or-random agreed to a docs PR in the thread.\n\nSize of `text` in bytes, static library built with the default modules and `CFLAGS=\"-g -O2\"`, plus the section flags in the last column:\n\n| program | no flags | sections + gc |\n|---|---|---|\n| signing only (ECDSA + Schnorr) | 1340145 | 131364 |\n| verifying only, `context_static` | 1340313 | 1128701 |\n| verifying only, `context_create` | 1340281 | 1234429 |\n\nMeasured with `size` and `nm` on the linked binaries (Debian trixie, aarch64, GCC 14.2, GNU ld 2.44); Autotools and CMake give identical sizes.\n",
